  "routeAdjustment": "Reuse original Riemann-Roch, native residue-field dimension one, the existing negative-degree LSpace theorem and existing linear differential coefficient map. Compose the coefficient, actual canonical residue and trace to obtain a globally linear residue map, avoiding the external partial evaluation-additivity development. Use a fixed actual analytic base place and a finite linear combination of normalized two-pole differentials instead of strong induction on divisor support. Split the dimension calculation, subspace existence and exact-order argument into checked declarations within the unchanged proof limits. The remaining period correction requires actual loop reciprocity; arithmetic class-field reciprocity in the repository is a different statement and does not discharge it.",
  "discharged": "Every actual original degree-zero divisor is realized as the exact residue divisor of an original differential with at most simple poles. Original Riemann-Roch and already proved negative-degree vanishing give a nonzero differential with simple poles at two specified distinct places and regular elsewhere. The actual canonical residue and trace form a linear map on original differentials. The original global residue theorem forces the two residues to sum to zero; the exact pole order makes them nonzero, permitting normalization to +1 and -1. A finite linear combination with the original divisor coefficients gives every prescribed residue. Degree zero cancels the auxiliary base-place term. The final consumer states literal original evaluation of the uniformizer times the differential coefficient, retaining the selected source contract. No Riemann-Roch, global residue, two-pole existence, normalization or third-kind existence premise remains.",
  "remaining": "Period correction to integral multiples of two pi i, the meromorphic exponential and original-function comparison still prevent closing the Abel converse. Period discreteness and exact original torsion cardinality, Qbar divisor-class comparison, Tate realization, rank-two Hecke/Frobenius and inertia comparison, arithmetic automorphy and higher symmetric-power continuation remain required. DUB-17--20 OPEN; 16/20. No acceptance gate closes here.",
  "production": "Scratch only; production promotion and verification pending.",
